    "q-86223": {
      "dom_id": "step-q86223",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Consider the equivalence relation $∼$ on $R,$ defined by $x∼y$ if $\\sqrt[3]{x}=\\sqrt[3]{y}.$ Which of the following are in the equivalence class $[-8]?$\n\nI. $-8$\n\nII. $8$\n\nIII. $2$",
      "worked_solution": "The equivalence class $[-8]$ consists of the elements that are equivalent to $-8$ under the given equivalence relation. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[-8] & =\\{x\\in R\\,|\\,x∼-8\\} \\\\  & =\\{x\\in R\\,|\\,\\sqrt[3]{x}=\\sqrt[3]{-8}\\} \\\\  & =\\{x\\in R\\,|\\,\\sqrt[3]{x}=-2\\} \\\\  & =\\{-8\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $-8$ is in $[-8],$ while $8$ and $2$ are not.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\".",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-86223-a",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "III only",
              "html": "III only"
            },
            {
              "option": "b",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-86223-b",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "I only",
              "html": "I only"
            },
            {
              "option": "c",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-86223-c",
              "type": "text",
