    "q-221766": {
      "dom_id": "step-q221766",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Consider the equivalence relation $∼$ on $R,$ defined by $x∼y$ if $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡y.$ Which of the following equivalence classes contain the element $4\\pi ?$\n\nI. $[-\\pi ]$\n\nII. $[\\frac{\\pi }{2}]$\n\nIII. $[3\\pi ]$",
      "worked_solution": "We have $4\\pi \\in [x]$ if $4\\pi ∼x.$ Using the definition of the given equivalence relation, we require\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\pi ) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ 0 & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's now consider each of the given equivalence classes.\n\n- $4\\pi \\in [-\\pi ]$ because $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\pi )=0\\,✓$\n\n- $4\\pi \\notin [\\frac{\\pi }{2}]$ because $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=1\\ne 0\\,\\times $\n\n- $4\\pi \\in [3\\pi ]$ because $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\pi )=0\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
