    "q-86228": {
      "dom_id": "step-q86228",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Consider the equivalence relation $∼$ on $R,$ defined by $x∼y$ if $\\sqrt[3]{x}=\\sqrt[3]{y}.$ Which of the following equivalence classes contain the element $64?$\n\nI. $[64]$\n\nII. $[-64]$\n\nIII. $[8]$",
      "worked_solution": "We have $64\\in [x]$ if $64∼x.$ Using the definition of the given equivalence relation, we require\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{64} & =\\sqrt[3]{x} \\\\ 4 & =\\sqrt[3]{x} \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{x} & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's now consider each of the given equivalence classes.\n\n- $64\\in [64]$ because $\\sqrt[3]{64}=4\\,✓$\n\n- $64\\notin [-64]$ because $\\sqrt[3]{-64}=-4\\ne 4\\,\\times $\n\n- $64\\notin [8]$ because $\\sqrt[3]{8}=2\\ne 4\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\".",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
