    "q-221719": {
      "dom_id": "step-q221719",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "Consider the equivalence relation $∼$ on $Z,$ defined by $x∼y$ if $7\\,|\\,(x-y).$ Which of the following equivalence classes contain the element $2?$\n\nI. $[1]$\n\nII. $[0]$\n\nIII. $[9]$",
      "worked_solution": "We have $2\\in [x]$ if $2∼x.$ Using the definition of the given equivalence relation, we require\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7\\,|\\,(2-x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's now consider each of the given equivalence classes.\n\n- $2\\notin [1]$ because $7∤(2-1)\\,\\times $\n\n- $2\\notin [0]$ because $7∤(2-0)\\,\\times $\n\n- $2\\in [9]$ because $7\\,|\\,(2-9)\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
